  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/de8e7bfd-613c-4dfa-bf36-70a166e1b6c2-image.png\" style=\"width: 230px; height: 157px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&Delta;</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>:</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>tan</mi><msup><mn>30</mn><mo>&deg;</mo></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></math> ......<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&Delta;</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>:</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>tan</mi><msup><mn>60</mn><mo>&deg;</mo></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;&nbsp; ......<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math><br /><br />From equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&amp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∵</mo></math> Speed is uniform<br /><br />Therefore, distance <math><mi>x</mi></math> walked by him in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>min</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br /><br />and distance <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> walked by him in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>min</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
